From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:12:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: Claude plan usage says when essential-traffic-only mode
 hides it

With CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC set, in the environment or in
the env block of the user settings, Claude Code never sends
GET /api/oauth/usage and answers the usage control with whatever it cached
earlier, so the plan usage shown was hours old and vanished once the
five-hour window reset. Instead of those numbers the server now names where
the variable is set and points to DISABLE_TELEMETRY, which keeps telemetry
off without that side effect. Claude Code treats an empty value as unset,
and so does the check.
